&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Current work on Partial differential equations are most focusing on numerical data. However, symbolic expressions are more valuable , in terms of explainable, and analyzable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This work focus on training a transformer model with symbolic ODE expressions. By replacing absolute positional embedding with tree positional embedding, and employed contrastive learning to learn mathematical equivalent but syntactic different expression (i.e., x+1 and 1+x)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Research Note-0</title><link>https://tina2023h.github.io/fragments/research/coding-on-multi-gpus/</link><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:29:35 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://tina2023h.github.io/fragments/research/coding-on-multi-gpus/</guid><description>&lt;h1 class="relative group"&gt;Lessons for multi-GPU training
