&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the learning note when I was trying to run experiments on multiple GPUs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Decide on batch size convention
 &lt;div id="decide-on-batch-size-convention" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 
 &lt;span
 class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
 &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#decide-on-batch-size-convention" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;/span&gt;
 
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Per-GPU batch size:what you pass to your dataloader(batch_size=..)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective batch size : per_gpu_batch_size * num_gpus*grad_accum_steps&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;grad_accum_steps: refers to how many steps updating the gradient, in my case grad_accum_steps=1&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>About me</title><link>https://tina2023h.github.io/fragments/posts/hello/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tina2023h.github.io/fragments/posts/hello/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Welcome to my website!
